#subtitle: Issues of taxation, budget, and tariffs.

= Fiscal Policy

As Finance Minister, Indalecio Prieto must balance the Republic's books - and the peseta's standing on the gold standard - against the demands of a coalition that wants land reform, public works, and social spending all at once.


@fiscal_menu

Upper-income tax rates: [+ upper_tax_rates : taxation +]

Lower-income tax rates: [+ lower_tax_rates : taxation +]

- @raise_rich: Increase taxes on the rich.
- @raise_poor
- @raise_overall: Increase overall taxes.
- @cut_rich
- @cut_poor
- @cut_overall: Cut overall taxes.
- @raise_progressive: Make the tax system more progressive by raising taxes on the rich and cutting them for the poor.
- @regressive
- @tariffs
- @root: Do not change the tax system.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@raise_progressive
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if lower_tax_rates < -5 : Lower-class tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if upper_tax_rates > 5 : Upper-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates >= -5 and upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe -= 3; urban_middle_psoe -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front; radical_relation -= 4; izq_rep_relation -= 2 if radical_ideology != "Left"; upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; urban_middle_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; smallholder_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1

Making the tax system more progressive is popular with our base, but it upsets our republican coalition partners and their own middle-class supporters, who now face higher taxes for participating in a government led from the left.

@raise_rich
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 3; industrial_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe -= 4; urban_middle_psoe -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front; coalition_dissent += 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 5; budget += 2; radical_relation -= 4; unemployed += 1; inflation -= 0.6; urban_middle_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; smallholder_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; economic_growth -= 0.4; left_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3

Raising taxes on the rich is popular among our base, but it alienates the propertied classes. Higher taxes also depress economic demand, which may mean more unemployment. Our republican coalition partners will face backlash from their own middle-class supporters for governing alongside a party that keeps raising their taxes.


@raise_poor
title: Raise consumption taxes, which disproportionately affect the poor.
subtitle: +2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 2; industrial_psoe -= 4; unemployed_psoe -= 4; lower_tax_rates += 1; industrial_psoe -= 6 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; unemployed_psoe -= 6 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; labor_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10

We have raised consumption taxes. This hurts our support among the workers and the unemployed.


@cut_overall
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -3 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 3 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 3; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; urban_middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); industrial_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 5*(1-dissent); ceda_relation += 5*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 1.5 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 1; economic_growth += 0.6

Cutting taxes benefits the rich and middle class most, since they pay more taxes than the working class. Our republican coalition partners are pleased at our orthodox economic course - it helps dispel any notion among their own supporters that they fail to represent the interests of the middle class while sharing government with us.

@cut_poor
title: Cut consumption taxes for the poor.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; lower_tax_rates -= 1; industrial_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.7 if unemployed >= 5; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.4; labor_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5

Our tax cuts disproportionately benefit the poor and working class.


@cut_rich
title: Cut income taxes for the rich.
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: budget >= 2 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: budget -= 2; upper_tax_rates -= 1; urban_middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 4*(1-dissent); ceda_relation += 4*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.7 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.4; labor_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5

We have reduced income and property taxes for the rich and middle class. The propertied parties approve of this orthodox course, and our coalition partners benefit from their participation in a government seen as friendly to the middle class.


@raise_overall
subtitle: +3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: budget += 3; urban_middle_psoe -= 4; smallholder_psoe -= 4; industrial_psoe -= 4; unemployed += 2; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if upper_tax_rates > 2; industrial_psoe -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; urban_middle_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; smallholder_psoe -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1

Raising taxes hurts our support among everyone who pays them, though our coalition partners are more supportive of the idea of shared sacrifice than of simply taxing the rich. Higher taxes also depress demand, which may mean more unemployment.

@regressive
title: Lower taxes on the rich, while raising consumption taxes (which affect the working class more).
subtitle: This does not change overall revenue. [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 : Rich tax rates are too low to cut anymore. ?] [? if lower_tax_rates > 5 : Lower-class tax rates are too high to increase. ?]
choose-if: lower_tax_rates <= 5 and upper_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: industrial_psoe -= 6; urban_middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 5; ceda_relation += 4; coalition_dissent -= 1 if (in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front) and coalition_dissent > 0; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; industrial_psoe -= 5 if lower_tax_rates >= 2; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; industrial_pce += 2; labor_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10

Our regressive taxation policy benefits the rich while hurting the poor and working class. Our republican coalition partners approve of this orthodox economic course, and the propertied classes are pleased.


@tariffs
title: Change tariffs instead.

Tariffs, or taxes on imports, are another way to finance our government.

Historically, <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> have favored free trade and low tariffs — workers in export-oriented industries and consumers of imported necessities both benefit from cheap imports. But Spain's smallholding farmers, especially wheat and olive growers, have long depended on protection from cheaper foreign grain and oil. Do the present economic circumstances change these calculations?

Current tariff level: [+ tariffs : taxation +]

- @raise_tariffs
- @lower_tariffs
- @fiscal_menu: Change domestic taxes instead of tariffs.
- @root: Do not change tariffs or taxes.
- @easy_discard

@raise_tariffs
title: Raise tariffs on imports.
subtitle: +2 budget. Other countries will retaliate by raising tariffs of their own. [? if tariffs > 5 : Further increases in tariffs will not raise revenue, as we have already nearly reached autarky. ?]
choose-if: tariffs <= 5
on-arrival: tariffs += 1; inflation += 1 if inflation > 0; inflation += 0.5 if inflation <= 0; unemployed += 1.5; budget += 2; industrial_psoe -= 7; unemployed_psoe -= 7; smallholder_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); ceda_relation += 3; radical_relation -= 2; izq_rep_relation -= 4; economic_growth -= 0.4

Raising tariffs pushes up prices for basic goods, feeding inflation and hurting consumption among the working class. Retaliatory tariffs from our trading partners reduce the competitiveness of Spanish exports - Catalan textiles above all - raising unemployment among industrial workers. They also sour our relations abroad, at a moment when the Republic can ill afford to be isolated.

On the other hand, smallholding farmers and some domestic industries benefit from higher tariffs, since they can now command higher prices without foreign competition undercutting them.

@lower_tariffs
title: Lower tariffs on imports.
choose-if: budget >= 2 and tariffs > -5
subtitle: -2 budget. [? if tariffs <= -5 : There are no tariffs left to cut. ?]
on-arrival: tariffs -= 1; budget -= 2; inflation -= 0.5; industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe -= 5; smallholder_monarchist += 4; smallholder_ceda += 2; economic_growth += 0.4

Lowering tariffs helps workers and the urban poor by reducing prices for basic necessities, and other countries are more willing to negotiate with us on other questions as a result. But smallholding farmers are hurt by cheap imported grain and oil, and many of them rally to the monarchist right and the CEDA in protest.
